.TH AD_RECORD 1 "2026-09-10" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_record \- record animation to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_record
.RI <oldfile> " <newfile> " <recording.dv>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_record
runs the ad_vim compute + postprocess + pace pipeline on an old/new
file pair and writes the resulting TIMED op stream (with delay, keep,
delete, insert ops) to a recording file. The recording can then be
replayed by
.B ad_replay
without needing the original new file \(em only the old file (initial
buffer) is needed at replay time.
.PP
Intermediate files are written to
.I /tmp/ad_raw.txt
and
.I /tmp/ad_post.txt
(overwritten each run).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show detailed help and exit.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <oldfile>
Path to the original/source file (initial buffer).
.TP
.I <newfile>
Path to the target file the animation should reach.
.TP
.I <recording.dv>
Path where the timed op stream will be saved.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_record old.py new.py /tmp/my_recording.dv
Record the animation that transforms old.py into new.py, saving the
timed op stream to
.IR /tmp/my_recording.dv .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_replay (1),
.BR ad_vim (1),
.BR ad_pipeline (1)
